    "q-150013": {
      "dom_id": "step-q150013",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14221961/assets/dcf7a2ea5b44f3f5ba7b1663f7979cdc3fc8c1036b6cc797904ffda77f1003bd.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the сurve is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$  assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14221961/assets/818ad935fd7aa592f00c23c9c77799d127449b4bb6ffacee4354e7acf39887d8.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14221961/assets/70e268a08195a92573f41927ae7de653837fca273f0c75cb951243a31ec660a2.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
